Strip an unsafe prefix again after tar --strip-components.
Leading slashes and ".." components were removed from a member name
before --strip-components removed its leading components, but not from
what was left, so a member named "dir//etc/passwd" was extracted as
"/etc/passwd", and on Windows "dir/C:/x" as "C:/x". A hard link's
target was shortened the same way, so the link could be made to a file
outside the current directory. Strip the name and the target again
after removing the components.

---
 archival/libarchive/data_extract_all.c |    4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

--- a/archival/libarchive/data_extract_all.c
+++ b/archival/libarchive/data_extract_all.c
@@ -63,6 +63,10 @@
 				hard_link++;
 			}
 		} while (--n != 0);
+		/* What is left of "dir//etc/passwd" is absolute */
+		dst_name = (char *)skip_unsafe_prefix(dst_name);
+		if (hard_link)
+			hard_link = (char *)skip_unsafe_prefix(hard_link);
 	}
 #endif
 #if ENABLE_FEATURE_PATH_TRAVERSAL_PROTECTION
